---

<Section spacing="large" aria-label="About our process">
  <div class="grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-2 md:gap-16">
    <Prose>
      <p>Most teams start a design system after the third button that looks almost, but not quite, like the other two. The cost is rarely the button; it is the conversation every time someone has to choose.</p>
      <p>A system turns those conversations into decisions made once, written down where people work.</p>
    </Prose>
    <Prose>
      <p>We work in short cycles with the people who will use the result:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Name the parts the way the team already talks about them.</li>
        <li>Write down when to use each one, and when not to.</li>
        <li>Let the build check what people forget.</li>
      </ul>
    </Prose>
  </div>
</Section>
